From: ProjectM TV maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Evaluate legacy per-pixel rows in original physical order

I12: original fixed-function mesh/projection visits physical rows opposite
 the current GL traversal. Evaluate legacy equation rows descending in
current storage, keeping X ascending and addressing each attribute by row.
Preserve actual custom path order, no-equation fill, one Q copy per frame,
ordinary/register/global-memory recurrence, RNG sequence, original raw
values, point/equation counts and prepared replay. No new pass or buffer.
Cache locality requires focused Native4K cost qualification.

diff --git a/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/PerPixelMesh.cpp b/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/PerPixelMesh.cpp
--- a/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/PerPixelMesh.cpp
+++ b/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/PerPixelMesh.cpp
@@ -256,12 +256,15 @@
     float sx = static_cast<float>(*perFrameContext.sx);
     float sy = static_cast<float>(*perFrameContext.sy);
-
+
-    int vertex = 0;
-
     // Can't make this multithreaded as per-pixel code may use gmegabuf or regXX vars.
     auto& vertices = m_warpMesh.Vertices();
-    for (int y = 0; y <= m_gridSizeY; y++)
-    {
+    // Original legacy equations traverse physical bottom-to-top, X ascending.
+    // Keep custom order and the cheap no-equation attribute fill unchanged.
+    const bool reverseRows = perPixelContext.perPixelCodeHandle && !m_warpShader;
+    for (int row = 0; row <= m_gridSizeY; row++)
+    {
+        const int y = reverseRows ? m_gridSizeY - row : row;
+        int vertex = y * (m_gridSizeX + 1);
         for (int x = 0; x <= m_gridSizeX; x++)
         {
             auto& curVertex = vertices[vertex];
